<h2>How to use Lato Spaces</h2>

<p>
  <code>lato_spaces</code> is a Rails engine for adding workspace/group selection to a Lato application.
  Users can belong to one or more groups, select the active group in the session, and scope application records to that group.
</p>

<h3>Installation</h3>

<p>Add Lato and Lato Spaces to the application Gemfile:</p>

<pre><code>gem "lato"
gem "lato_spaces"</code></pre>

<p>Install dependencies, copy engine files, install migrations, and migrate the database:</p>

<pre><code>bundle
rails lato_spaces:install:application
rails lato_spaces:install:migrations
rails db:migrate</code></pre>

<p>Mount the engine in <code>config/routes.rb</code>:</p>

<pre><code>Rails.application.routes.draw do
  mount LatoSpaces::Engine =&gt; "/lato-spaces"

  # ...
end</code></pre>

<p>Import styles in <code>app/assets/stylesheets/application.scss</code>:</p>

<pre><code>@import "lato_spaces/application";</code></pre>

<p>Import JavaScript in <code>app/javascript/application.js</code>:</p>

<pre><code>import "lato_spaces/application"</code></pre>

<div class="alert alert-info mt-3">
  <h4 class="alert-heading">Install task output</h4>
  <p>
    <code>rails lato_spaces:install:application</code> copies overridable partials to
    <code>app/views/layouts/lato_spaces</code> and copies
    <code>app/models/concerns/lato_spaces_membership_application.rb</code> into the host application.
  </p>
</div>

<h3>Configuration</h3>

<p>Create or update a Lato initializer:</p>

<pre><code>LatoSpaces.configure do |config|
  config.setgroup_redirect_path = :dashboard_path
  config.setgroup_auto_after_login = false
  config.setgroup_auto_after_login_if_single = true

  config.group_icon = "bi bi-people-fill"
  config.group_params = %i[name]
  config.membership_params = %i[email]

  config.permit_group_creation = false
  config.permit_group_management = false
  config.permit_group_preferred = false
end</code></pre>

<div class="table-responsive">
  <table class="table table-striped align-middle">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Option</th>
        <th>Default</th>
        <th>Purpose</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>setgroup_redirect_path</code></td>
        <td><code>nil</code></td>
        <td>Named route called after selecting a group. Example: <code>:dashboard_path</code>.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>setgroup_auto_after_login</code></td>
        <td><code>false</code></td>
        <td>Automatically selects the first available group when the user enters the Spaces root.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>setgroup_auto_after_login_if_single</code></td>
        <td><code>false</code></td>
        <td>Automatically selects the group only when the user has exactly one group.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>group_icon</code></td>
        <td><code>"bi bi-people-fill"</code></td>
        <td>Bootstrap Icons class used for groups.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>group_params</code></td>
        <td><code>%i[name]</code></td>
        <td>Strong parameters allowed when creating/updating groups.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>membership_params</code></td>
        <td><code>%i[email]</code></td>
        <td>Strong parameters allowed when creating memberships.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>permit_group_creation</code></td>
        <td><code>false</code></td>
        <td>Allows non-admin users to create groups.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>permit_group_management</code></td>
        <td><code>false</code></td>
        <td>Allows non-admin users to manage their groups and memberships.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>permit_group_preferred</code></td>
        <td><code>false</code></td>
        <td>Allows users to mark one membership group as preferred.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<h3>Admin and permissions</h3>

<p>
  The migrations add <code>lato_spaces_admin</code> to <code>Lato::User</code>.
  Admin users can list all groups and manage every group. Non-admin users can access only groups where they have a membership.
</p>

<pre><code>user = Lato::User.find_by(email: "admin@example.com")
user.update!(lato_spaces_admin: true)</code></pre>

<p>
  Non-admin access to creation, management, and preferred group selection depends on the configuration flags shown above.
</p>

<h3>Protect controllers with selected group</h3>

<p>Include <code>LatoSpaces::Groupable</code> in controllers that need group-aware access:</p>

<pre><code>class ApplicationController &lt; Lato::ApplicationController
  include LatoSpaces::Groupable

  # ...
end</code></pre>

<p>
  To require group selection before an action, call <code>authenticate_group</code>.
  If no group is selected, the user is redirected to the Lato Spaces root.
</p>

<pre><code>class ProductsController &lt; ApplicationController
  before_action :authenticate_session
  before_action :authenticate_group

  def index
    group_id = @session.get(:spaces_group_id)
    @products = Product.for_lato_spaces_group(group_id)
  end
end</code></pre>

<p>The selected group id is stored in the Lato session payload:</p>

<pre><code>group_id = @session.get(:spaces_group_id)</code></pre>

<h3>Group selection flow</h3>

<p>
  The engine root lists groups available to the current user. Selecting a group calls
  <code>POST /lato-spaces/setgroup/:id</code>, stores <code>spaces_group_id</code> in the encrypted Lato session cookie,
  then redirects to <code>setgroup_redirect_path</code> if configured.
</p>

<pre><code># Deselect current group from application code
session_group_destroy

# Select group from application code
session_group_create(group.id)</code></pre>

<h3>Memberships and invitations</h3>

<p>
  A group has many memberships. A membership can reference either an existing <code>Lato::User</code>
  or a pending <code>Lato::Invitation</code>.
</p>

<ul>
  <li>If the membership email matches an existing user, the membership links to that user.</li>
  <li>If no user exists, Lato Spaces creates or reuses a <code>Lato::Invitation</code>.</li>
  <li>When an invitation is accepted, memberships are automatically moved from the invitation to the new user.</li>
  <li>Destroying a Lato invitation or user removes related memberships.</li>
</ul>

<pre><code>group = LatoSpaces::Group.find(1)
membership = group.lato_spaces_memberships.create!(email: "member@example.com")
membership.send_invite if membership.lato_invitation.present?</code></pre>

<p>Preferred group can be set from a membership:</p>

<pre><code>membership.set_preferred</code></pre>

<h3>Usage on models</h3>

<p>Any model can be associated with one or more groups using <code>LatoSpaces::Associable</code>:</p>

<pre><code>class Product &lt; ApplicationRecord
  include LatoSpaces::Associable

  # ...
end</code></pre>

<p>Available associations, helpers, operations, and scopes:</p>

<pre><code>product = Product.first

product.lato_spaces_associations
product.lato_spaces_groups
product.lato_spaces_group
product.lato_spaces_group_id

product.add_to_lato_spaces_group(1)
product.remove_from_lato_spaces_group(1)
product.switch_lato_spaces_group(1)

Product.for_lato_spaces_group(1)
Product.with_lato_spaces_groups
Product.without_lato_spaces_groups</code></pre>

<h3>Require group association on create</h3>

<p>
  Add <code>LatoSpaces::AssociableRequired</code> when the model must always be created with a group.
  The concern validates <code>lato_spaces_group_id</code> on create and creates the association after commit.
</p>

<pre><code>class Product &lt; ApplicationRecord
  include LatoSpaces::Associable
  include LatoSpaces::AssociableRequired

  # ...
end

product = Product.create!(name: "Product 1", lato_spaces_group_id: 1)</code></pre>

<div class="alert alert-warning mt-3">
  <h4 class="alert-heading">Destroy behavior</h4>
  <p>
    With <code>AssociableRequired</code>, destroying a <code>LatoSpaces::Association</code> also destroys the associated item.
    Use this concern only for records that should not exist outside a group.
  </p>
</div>

<h3>Limit a model to one group</h3>

<p>
  Add <code>LatoSpaces::AssociableUnique</code> when a record can belong to only one group.
  The concern aborts creation of additional associations. Use <code>switch_lato_spaces_group</code> to move the record.
</p>

<pre><code>class Product &lt; ApplicationRecord
  include LatoSpaces::Associable
  include LatoSpaces::AssociableUnique

  # ...
end

product.switch_lato_spaces_group(2)</code></pre>

<h3>Recommended CRUD pattern</h3>

<p>Filter lists by the selected group and assign new records to that group:</p>

<pre><code>class ProductsController &lt; ApplicationController
  before_action :authenticate_session
  before_action :authenticate_group

  def index
    @products = Product.for_lato_spaces_group(@session.get(:spaces_group_id))
  end

  def create_action
    @product = Product.new(product_params.merge(
      lato_spaces_group_id: @session.get(:spaces_group_id)
    ))

    if @product.save
      redirect_to products_path, notice: "Product created successfully"
    else
      render :create, status: :unprocessable_entity
    end
  end

  private

  def product_params
    params.require(:product).permit(:name)
  end
end</code></pre>

<h3>Customize groups, memberships, and layout content</h3>

<p>The install task copies these partials into the host application:</p>

<ul>
  <li><code>app/views/layouts/lato_spaces/_group-informations_content.html.erb</code></li>
  <li><code>app/views/layouts/lato_spaces/_group-form-extra_content.html.erb</code></li>
  <li><code>app/views/layouts/lato_spaces/_membership-form-extra_content.html.erb</code></li>
</ul>

<p>
  Edit those files to add custom information or fields to Lato Spaces pages.
  If custom fields are added to group or membership forms, also extend
  <code>group_params</code> or <code>membership_params</code> in the initializer.
</p>

<p>
  The install task also copies <code>LatoSpacesMembershipApplication</code> into the host application.
  Use it to add custom relations, scopes, validations, or helpers to all memberships.
</p>

<pre><code>module LatoSpacesMembershipApplication
  extend ActiveSupport::Concern

  included do
    # Add custom validations, relations, or scopes here.
  end

  # Add custom methods here.
end</code></pre>
